# WarnFlux: bring up the packet link on the modem's DATA interface.
#
# This script runs on /dev/serial/by-id/usb-HUAWEI_Technology_HUAWEI_Mobile-if00-port0
# (the interface pppd accepts on this stick). The station's SMS session keeps the
# other AT interface (if04, mapped into the container as /dev/modem-4), so
# dialling here never locks the panel out of the SIM.
ABORT BUSY
ABORT 'NO CARRIER'
ABORT 'NO DIALTONE'
ABORT ERROR
ABORT 'NO ANSWER'
TIMEOUT 30

# This interface DOES answer AT (the silent one is if03, see README).
# The packet domain is attached by hand: this modem never attaches by itself
# (AT+CGATT? answers 0 on a fresh boot), and without it the dial ends in
# NO CARRIER. Measured working on the production stick with the Orange SIM
# (2026-11-10): CONNECT, then IPCP grants a 10.x.x.x address.
'' AT
OK ATE0
OK AT+CGATT=1
OK ATD*99***1#
CONNECT ''
